T:What it is
T:The ocean is
T:the body of
T:salt water
T:that covers
T:approximatel
T:70.8% of
T:Earth. The
T:ocean is
T:conventional
T:divided into
T:large bodies
T:of water,
T:which are
T:also
T:referred to
T:as oceans,
T:and are
T:themselves
T:mostly
T:divided into
T:seas, gulfs
T:and
T:subsequent
T:bodies of
T:water. The
T:ocean
T:contains 97%
T:of Earth's
T:water and is
T:the primary
T:component of
T:Earth's
T:hydrosphere,
T:acting as a
T:huge
T:reservoir of
T:heat for
T:Earth's
T:energy
T:budget, as
T:well as for
T:its carbon
T:cycle and
T:water cycle,
T:forming the
T:basis for
T:climate and
T:weather
T:patterns
T:worldwide.
T:The ocean is
T:essential to
T:life on
T:Earth,
T:harbouring
T:most of
T:Earth's
T:animals and
T:protist
T:life. It
T:originated
T:photosynthes
T:and
T:therefore
T:Earth's
T:atmospheric
T:oxygen, and
T:still
T:supplies
T:half of it.
